{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012KXnsjNMxXJmEVnKrdeyNT","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd025-unexpand\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/unexpand: Convert Spaces to Tabs\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  macOS BSD unexpand converts only leading spaces, while GNU unexpand adds -a to convert\n6\t  all runs of spaces in the line. Scripts that compact whitespace in structured files\n7\t  depend on the GNU behavior. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference\n8\t  binary (gunexpand, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all flag combinations,\n9\t  verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n10\t\n11\tgoals:\n12\t  - G1: Convert runs of spaces to tabs where alignment permits, matching GNU unexpand behavior.\n13\t  - G2: By default, convert only leading whitespace (spaces and tabs at the start of each line).\n14\t  - G3: Support -a to convert all occurrences of two or more spaces, not just leading whitespace.\n15\t  - G4: Support -t to configure tab stop positions as a single interval or a list, matching the srd024-expand convention.\n16\t\n17\trequirements:\n18\t  R1:\n19\t    title: Default behavior (leading whitespace only)\n20\t    items:\n21\t      - R1.1:\n22\t          text: By default, unexpand must replace leading spaces (and mixed leading spaces and tabs) with tabs only when doing so advances to the same column position. Tabs are preferred over spaces when a run of spaces reaches a tab stop exactly.\n23\t      - R1.2:\n24\t          text: Non-leading whitespace must be written unchanged in default mode. Characters after the first non-whitespace character on a line are not converted.\n25\t      - R1.3:\n26\t          text: A run of spaces that does not exactly reach a tab stop must be kept as spaces; unexpand must not insert a tab that would overshoot the column.\n27\t      - R1.4:\n28\t          text: Existing tab characters in leading whitespace count toward the column position as in expand; they do not prevent further tab substitution.\n29\t\n30\t  R2:\n31\t    title: Convert all whitespace (-a)\n32\t    items:\n33\t      - R2.1:\n34\t          text: -a must convert all runs of spaces (not just leading) where replacement with tabs aligns to a tab stop. The rule is the same as R1.1 applied at every column position in the line, not only at the start.\n35\t      - R2.2:\n36\t          text: A single space that does not reach a tab stop must be kept as a space even with -a.\n37\t      - R2.3:\n38\t          text: The first non-space, non-tab character on the line does not stop the conversion; -a processes the entire line.\n39\t\n40\t  R3:\n41\t    title: Custom tab stops (-t)\n42\t    items:\n43\t      - R3.1:\n44\t          text: -t N must set a uniform tab stop interval of N columns. -t LIST must set absolute tab stop positions. Behavior mirrors srd024-expand R2.1 and R2.2 for tab stop resolution.\n45\t      - R3.2:\n46\t          text: When past the last explicit tab stop in a LIST, remaining spaces are kept as-is (no tab can be inserted beyond the last defined stop).\n47\t      - R3.3:\n48\t          text: -t implies -a; when custom tab stops are given, all whitespace in the line is subject to conversion, not just leading whitespace.\n49\t\n50\t  R4:\n51\t    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n52\t    items:\n53\t      - R4.1:\n54\t          text: Must exit 0 when all inputs are processed successfully.\n55\t      - R4.2:\n56\t          text: Must exit 1 when any input file cannot be opened, printing the error to stderr. Processing continues for remaining files.\n57\t      - R4.3:\n58\t          text: Must exit 1 when a write error occurs on stdout.\n59\t      - R4.4:\n60\t          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n61\t\n62\tnon_goals:\n63\t  - cmd/unexpand is not the exact inverse of expand for all inputs; the asymmetry (leading-only default, space-only conversion) is intentional and matches GNU behavior.\n64\t  - cmd/unexpand does not implement Unicode grapheme width; each byte counts as one column under LC_ALL=C.\n65\t\n66\tacceptance_criteria:\n67\t  - id: AC1\n68\t    criterion: \"printf '        text' | unexpand produces '\\\\ttext' (leading 8 spaces become one tab), matching gunexpand.\"\n69\t    traces:\n70\t      - R1.1\n71\t      - R1.2\n72\t      - R1.3\n73\t      - R1.4\n74\t  - id: AC2\n75\t    criterion: \"printf '        text' | unexpand -a produces '\\\\ttext' (all-mode still converts leading spaces), matching gunexpand -a.\"\n76\t    traces:\n77\t      - R2.1\n78\t      - R2.2\n79\t      - R2.3\n80\t      - R3.3\n81\t  - id: AC3\n82\t    criterion: \"printf 'a        b' | unexpand produces 'a        b' (non-leading spaces unchanged in default mode), matching gunexpand.\"\n83\t    traces:\n84\t      - R1.1\n85\t      - R1.2\n86\t      - R1.3\n87\t      - R1.4\n88\t  - id: AC4\n89\t    criterion: \"printf 'a        b' | unexpand -a produces 'a\\\\tb' (non-leading spaces converted with -a), matching gunexpand -a.\"\n90\t    traces:\n91\t      - R2.1\n92\t      - R2.2\n93\t      - R2.3\n94\t      - R3.3\n95\t  - id: AC5\n96\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gunexpand passes for all required test cases.\"\n97\t    traces:\n98\t      - R1.1\n99\t      - R1.2\n100\t      - R1.3\n101\t      - R1.4\n102\t  - id: AC6\n103\t    criterion: \"cmd/unexpand compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n104\t    traces:\n105\t      - R1.1\n106\t      - R1.2\n107\t      - R1.3\n108\t      - R1.4\n109\t      - R2.1\n110\t      - R2.2\n111\t      - R2.3\n112\t      - R3.1\n113\t      - R3.2\n114\t      - R3.3\n115\t      - R4.1\n116\t      - R4.2\n117\t      - R4.3\n118\t      - R4.4\n119\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2ba4d68e-6e98-457c-a01f-730b17272aed","uuid":"52db1af4-2275-4dc8-a0c0-0509200bb5cb","timestamp":"2026-05-15T14:47:28.834Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5277/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd025-unexpand.yaml","content":"id: srd025-unexpand\ntitle: \"cmd/unexpand: Convert Spaces to Tabs\"\n\nproblem: |\n  macOS BSD unexpand converts only leading spaces, while GNU unexpand adds -a to convert\n  all runs of spaces in the line. Scripts that compact whitespace in structured files\n  depend on the GNU behavior. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference\n  binary (gunexpand, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all flag combinations,\n  verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Convert runs of spaces to tabs where alignment permits, matching GNU unexpand behavior.\n  - G2: By default, convert only leading whitespace (spaces and tabs at the start of each line).\n  - G3: Support -a to convert all occurrences of two or more spaces, not just leading whitespace.\n  - G4: Support -t to configure tab stop positions as a single interval or a list, matching the srd024-expand convention.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Default behavior (leading whitespace only)\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: By default, unexpand must replace leading spaces (and mixed leading spaces and tabs) with tabs only when doing so advances to the same column position. Tabs are preferred over spaces when a run of spaces reaches a tab stop exactly.\n      - R1.2:\n          text: Non-leading whitespace must be written unchanged in default mode. Characters after the first non-whitespace character on a line are not converted.\n      - R1.3:\n          text: A run of spaces that does not exactly reach a tab stop must be kept as spaces; unexpand must not insert a tab that would overshoot the column.\n      - R1.4:\n          text: Existing tab characters in leading whitespace count toward the column position as in expand; they do not prevent further tab substitution.\n\n  R2:\n    title: Convert all whitespace (-a)\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: -a must convert all runs of spaces (not just leading) where replacement with tabs aligns to a tab stop. The rule is the same as R1.1 applied at every column position in the line, not only at the start.\n      - R2.2:\n          text: A single space that does not reach a tab stop must be kept as a space even with -a.\n      - R2.3:\n          text: The first non-space, non-tab character on the line does not stop the conversion; -a processes the entire line.\n\n  R3:\n    title: Custom tab stops (-t)\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: -t N must set a uniform tab stop interval of N columns. -t LIST must set absolute tab stop positions. Behavior mirrors srd024-expand R2.1 and R2.2 for tab stop resolution.\n      - R3.2:\n          text: When past the last explicit tab stop in a LIST, remaining spaces are kept as-is (no tab can be inserted beyond the last defined stop).\n      - R3.3:\n          text: -t implies -a; when custom tab stops are given, all whitespace in the line is subject to conversion, not just leading whitespace.\n\n  R4:\n    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n    items:\n      - R4.1:\n          text: Must exit 0 when all inputs are processed successfully.\n      - R4.2:\n          text: Must exit 1 when any input file cannot be opened, printing the error to stderr. Processing continues for remaining files.\n      - R4.3:\n          text: Must exit 1 when a write error occurs on stdout.\n      - R4.4:\n          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/unexpand is not the exact inverse of expand for all inputs; the asymmetry (leading-only default, space-only conversion) is intentional and matches GNU behavior.\n  - cmd/unexpand does not implement Unicode grapheme width; each byte counts as one column under LC_ALL=C.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"printf '        text' | unexpand produces '\\\\ttext' (leading 8 spaces become one tab), matching gunexpand.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"printf '        text' | unexpand -a produces '\\\\ttext' (all-mode still converts leading spaces), matching gunexpand -a.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R3.3\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"printf 'a        b' | unexpand produces 'a        b' (non-leading spaces unchanged in default mode), matching gunexpand.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"printf 'a        b' | unexpand -a produces 'a\\\\tb' (non-leading spaces converted with -a), matching gunexpand -a.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R3.3\n  - id: AC5\n    criterion: \"Differential test against gunexpand passes for all required test cases.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n  - id: AC6\n    criterion: \"cmd/unexpand compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n      - R4.1\n      - R4.2\n      - R4.3\n      - R4.4\n","numLines":119,"startLine":1,"totalLines":119}}}
