{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is running an automated \"stitch\" task (#5277) from a code generation pipeline. The task is to implement srd025-unexpand requirements R4.1-R4.4 (Exit codes and SIGPIPE) in the go-unix-utils project. Specifically:\n   - R4.1: Exit 0 when all inputs are processed successfully\n   - R4.2: Exit 1 when any input file cannot be opened, printing error to stderr, continuing for remaining files\n   - R4.3: Exit 1 when a write error occurs on stdout\n   - R4.4: Handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler\n   \n   Both `cmd/unexpand/main.go` and `cmd/unexpand/unexpand_test.go` must be modified. Acceptance criteria require: code compiles, go vet passes, go test passes (with graceful skip if gunexpand not in PATH).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern using `testutils.BuildBinary` and `testutils.RunDiffTests`\n   - Reference binary is `gunexpand` from Homebrew GNU coreutils\n   - SIGPIPE handling via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - Exit code conventions: 0 for success, 1 for errors\n   - `LC_ALL=C` required in test Env fields\n   - Write errors on buffered stdout must be detected and cause exit 1\n   - No git commands allowed; git managed externally by orchestrator\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd025-unexpand.yaml**\n     - Source of truth for requirements. R4 section (lines 50-61) defines exit code and SIGPIPE requirements.\n     - R4.1: exit 0 on success; R4.2: exit 1 on file open error, continue processing; R4.3: exit 1 on stdout write error; R4.4: SIGPIPE via InstallSIGPIPEHandler\n\n   - **cmd/unexpand/main.go** (229 lines, existing implementation)\n     - Already has R4.4: `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` on line 19\n     - Already has R4.2: file open error handling on lines 35-39 with stderr message and `exitCode = 1`\n     - Already has R4.1: `os.Exit(exitCode)` on line 48 where exitCode defaults to 0\n     - Partial R4.3: `w.Flush()` error on lines 45-47 causes `os.Exit(1)`, BUT the `unexpand()` function (lines 128-192) ignores all `w.WriteByte()` errors — write errors mid-stream are not detected/propagated\n     - Key function signatures:\n       ```go\n       func main()\n       func parseArgs(args []string) (tabStops, bool, []string, error)\n       func parseTabStops(val string) (tabStops, error)\n       func unexpand(r io.Reader, w *bufio.Writer, stops tabStops, allMode bool)\n       func nextTabStop(col int, stops tabStops) int\n       func pastLastStop(col int, stops tabStops) bool\n       func emitCompacted(w *bufio.Writer, startCol int, count int, stops tabStops)\n       ```\n\n   - **cmd/unexpand/unexpand_test.go** (234 lines, existing tests)\n     - Has TestDiff function with tests for R1.1-R1.4, R2.1-R2.3, R3.1-R3.3\n     - No tests for R4.x requirements yet\n     - Uses pattern: `goBin := testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")`, `refBin, err := exec.LookPath(\"gunexpand\")`, `testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)`\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet — only file reads were completed before the summary was requested.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Identified that R4.4 (SIGPIPE) and R4.2 (file open error) are already implemented in the existing code\n   - Identified that R4.1 (exit 0 on success) is already implemented via the exitCode variable defaulting to 0\n   - Identified the gap for R4.3: the `unexpand()` function doesn't check or propagate write errors from `w.WriteByte()` calls. The `w.Flush()` at the end catches buffered write errors, but proper R4.3 implementation may need the unexpand function to return an error or check write results\n   - Need to add differential test cases for R4.1-R4.4 to the test file\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - The initial message is the full stitch task description with all project context, SRD references, execution constitution, coding standards, constraints, and the specific task to implement R4.1-R4.4\n   - Second user message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" — requesting a summary of the conversation\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Modify `cmd/unexpand/main.go` to fully implement R4.3 (write error detection on stdout)\n   - Add differential test cases for R4.1-R4.4 to `cmd/unexpand/unexpand_test.go`\n   - Run `go build -o bin/unexpand ./cmd/unexpand/` to verify compilation\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/unexpand/` to check for issues\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/unexpand/ -count=1` to verify all tests pass\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading all three required files (SRD, main.go, test file) and was about to plan the implementation approach. I had identified what already exists and what gaps remain. The next step was to:\n   \n   a) Modify `cmd/unexpand/main.go` to properly handle R4.3 write errors — likely by checking the error from `w.Flush()` (which is already done) and potentially making the `unexpand()` function more robust about write error propagation. The existing Flush check on lines 45-47 may already suffice since bufio.Writer accumulates errors.\n   \n   b) Add test cases to `cmd/unexpand/unexpand_test.go` for R4.1-R4.4, particularly:\n      - R4.1: A normal success case (exit 0) — many existing tests already verify this implicitly\n      - R4.2: Pass a nonexistent filename as argument (should exit 1 with stderr message)\n      - R4.3: Difficult to test differentially but may test via write to closed pipe\n      - R4.4: SIGPIPE test case\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Implement the R4.1-R4.4 changes. The task description says: \"Implement srd025-unexpand requirement R4.1 exactly as specified in the SRD\" through R4.4. I need to:\n   1. Analyze whether existing main.go already satisfies R4.1, R4.2, R4.3, R4.4 or needs modifications (R4.3 write error handling may need improvement)\n   2. Write the code changes to main.go\n   3. Add test cases to unexpand_test.go with DiffTest entries for R4.x scenarios (file not found, successful processing exit code, etc.)\n   4. Build and test to verify acceptance criteria AC1-AC5\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5277/2ba4d68e-6e98-457c-a01f-730b17272aed.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2ba4d68e-6e98-457c-a01f-730b17272aed","uuid":"e18460af-6a75-4773-97f2-7d45497c8139","timestamp":"2026-05-15T14:48:24.460Z","isSynthetic":true}
